            "description": "Watch Hapoel Tel Aviv vs Ludogorets highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 23, 2026. Hapoel Tel Aviv and Ludogorets locked horns in a crucial UEFA Europa Conference League clash on July 23, 2026, with everything to play for in a high-stakes European encounter. The match promised tactical intrigue and physical intensity as both clubs aimed to assert their dominance on the continental stage. Tight Opening and the Breakthrough The match began with a cautious approach from both sides, as Hapoel Tel Aviv and Ludogorets looked to find their rhythm under the European lights. The physical nature of the contest became apparent early on when Filip Kaloc received a yellow card in the 37th minute, a sign of the growing tension in midfield. However, just as the first half seemed destined to end goalless, the home side found their breakthrough. In the 45th minute, Stav Turiel delivered a precise ball to Omri Altman , who made no mistake in finding the back of the net to give his side the lead right before the interval. Tactical Shifts and Late Drama The second half saw both managers turn to their benches to influence the game's momentum. Ludogorets introduced fresh legs in the 63rd minute, bringing on Kwadwo Duah , Bernard Tekpetey , and Ivaylo Chochev , while Hapoel responded by bringing on Roei Alkukin . The game became increasingly fractious, with Petar Stanic , Chico , and Chochev all entering the referee's book as the intensity ramped up. Despite the pressure from the visitors, Hapoel Tel Aviv maintained their composure and looked dangerous on the counter-attack. In the 89th minute, the victory was finally secured. Substitute Roei Alkukin turned provider, setting up Chico , who clinically finished to double the lead and spark celebrations among the home fans. Although the final moments saw Bernard Tekpetey pick up a late yellow card in stoppage time, the result was never in doubt. The final whistle confirmed a professional and hard-fought victory for the hosts, leaving the visitors to reflect on missed opportunities."
